+## Symbolic links
+
+Archive files may contain symbolic links. By default these are skipped,
+like symlinks in any other backend. If `-l` / `--links` is in use then
+they are shown with a `.rclonelink` suffix on their name, and reading
+one returns the link target, so copying to a destination which supports
+symlinks recreates them.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2025-10-27 14:39:20.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2025-10-27 14:39:20.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Oct 27 14:39 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular archive member whose name happens to end in `.rclonelink`
+stays a regular file.
+
 ## Hashes
 
 Which hash is supported depends on the archive type. Zip files use
